    <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-glance__callout">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-glance__callout-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18h6"/><path d="M10 22h4"/><path d="M15.09 14c.18-.98.65-1.74 1.41-2.5A4.65 4.65 0 0 0 18 8 6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .23 2.23 1.5 3.5A4.61 4.61 0 0 1 8.91 14"/></svg></span>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-glance__callout-text"><strong>Worth knowing:</strong> two claims that circulate about these products are wrong. The famous "300 question limit" on Google Forms is a misreading of 300 pieces of content, and Google publishes no question cap at all. Microsoft is the one with a hard limit, at 200 questions per form.</p>
