<section class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__container">

    <header class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__header">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__eyebrow">The honest read</span>
      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__heading">Where does each one fall short?</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__sub">Both are free with an account and good enough for a poll. These are the ceilings that send teams looking.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__grid">
<article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__card"><div aria-hidden="true" style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:8px;background:#f7f3ff;border:1px solid #e4d7ff;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#6941c6;margin-bottom:14px;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg></div><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__title">Neither branches properly</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__body">Google branches at section level and only from multiple choice or dropdown questions. Microsoft branches per question but forward only. Neither documents answer piping or compound rules.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__card"><div aria-hidden="true" style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:8px;background:#f7f3ff;border:1px solid #e4d7ff;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#6941c6;margin-bottom:14px;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m12 14 4-4"/><path d="M3.34 19a10 10 0 1 1 17.32 0"/></svg></div><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__title">Microsoft caps questions and degrades at scale</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__body">200 questions per form and 400 forms. Past 50,000 responses it falls back to CSV only, losing summary charts, individual response view, and manual grading.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__card"><div aria-hidden="true" style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:8px;background:#f7f3ff;border:1px solid #e4d7ff;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#6941c6;margin-bottom:14px;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg></div><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__title">Microsoft's free tier stops at 200 responses</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__body">On a personal account each form accepts 200 responses free, 1,000 on paid. Google Forms publishes no response cap on a consumer account.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__card"><div aria-hidden="true" style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:8px;background:#f7f3ff;border:1px solid #e4d7ff;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#6941c6;margin-bottom:14px;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="2" y1="10" x2="22" y2="10"/></svg></div><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__title">Neither takes payments</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-why-leave__body">No payment field in either product, so anything transactional needs a separate tool. Microsoft's own docs point users to Dynamics 365 Customer Voice once they outgrow Forms.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
