<section class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__container">

    <header class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__header">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__eyebrow">Migration</span>
      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__heading">How do you move from either one to Formester?</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__sub">Three steps, and the same process works whichever suite you are on.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__grid">
<article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__title">Export your responses</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__body">In Google Forms, open Responses and link or download the Sheets file. In Microsoft Forms, open the Responses tab and choose Open results in Excel, then take a downloaded copy rather than the live-connected workbook.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__hint"><strong>Time:</strong> about five minutes per form.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__title">Rebuild with AI</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__body">Paste your question list into Formester's AI generator or describe the form in a sentence. It drafts the questions, pages, and design in about half a minute, then you add the branching you could not build before.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__hint"><strong>Input options:</strong> plain prompt, pasted question list, or PDF upload.</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__step"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__title">Share the new link</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__body">Publish the Formester link or embed, send one test response, and keep the old form open for a week as a fallback before you close it.</p><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-switch__hint"><strong>Worth checking:</strong> Google Sheets permissions do not stay in sync with form permissions after creation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
      </div>
    </section>

