      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__heading">When should you stay on one of them?</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__sub">Both are genuinely the right answer in some situations. Three of them.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__grid">
<article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2v20"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__title">It only needs to be free and quick</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__desc">For a poll, an RSVP, or a class quiz, either is free and already in your account.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__list"><li>Google Forms is free with any Google account and publishes no response cap</li><li>Microsoft Forms is free with a personal account up to 200 responses per form</li><li>Formester's free plan is unlimited but carries our branding until Personal</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose either suite for simple, internal, one-off forms</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__title">The data must stay in your tenant</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__desc">Microsoft's live-connected Excel in OneDrive or SharePoint keeps responses under existing governance.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__list"><li>Responses land in the tenant with your existing access controls and retention</li><li>Forms is named in Microsoft's commercial in-scope list, with a BAA available by default via the DPA</li><li>External users cannot refresh the connected workbook, which is a real limitation</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose Microsoft Forms when tenant governance is the requirement</p></article><article class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__card"><span class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__cicon" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20V10"/><path d="M18 20V4"/><path d="M6 20v-4"/></svg></span><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__title">You grade quizzes at scale</h3><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__desc">Google documents the richer grading analytics of the two.</p><ul class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__list"><li>Frequently missed questions, average, median, and range of scores</li><li>Graphs marked with correct answers and per-question grading</li><li>Microsoft's manual grading stops working past 50,000 responses</li></ul><p class="fmstr-cmp-gvm-when-wins__tradeoff">Choose Google Forms for quizzes and grading</p></article>
